      "content": "I can see why the weight of losing your former self feels so suffocating. It's as if your entire existence was predicated on being this perfect, idealized version of yourself, and now that's all gone. The pain of confronting that imperfection is making you feel like seeking a way to erase or escape from the reality of your current state. But self-preservation often requires facing this pain head-on.",
      "source": "target",
